IEC 62443 is the standards series for cybersecurity in industrial automation systems. It divides responsibility between **manufacturers**, *integrators* and asset owners.

## Parts of the series

- 62443-1 covers concepts and models
- 62443-2 targets the asset owner
- 62443-3 covers system requirements and security levels
- 62443-4 describes secure product development

## Security levels

1. SL 1 protection against unintentional events
2. SL 2 protection against simple intentional attacks
3. SL 3 protection against sophisticated attacks
4. SL 4 protection against state-level actors

### Zones and conduits

> Divide the system into zones with similar security needs and limit communication between zones.

| Level | Meaning |
| ----- | ------- |
| SL 1 | Baseline |
| SL 2 | Normal level for most facilities |

```sh
search "IEC 62443" --scope ot
```

